const tables={
articles:{title:"Definite articles · der/die/das",head:["Case","Masculine","Feminine","Neuter","Plural"],rows:[
["Nominativ","der","die","das","die"],["Akkusativ","den","die","das","die"],["Dativ","dem","der","dem","den (+n noun often)"],["Genitiv","des (+s noun)","der","des (+s noun)","der"]],note:"Memorise the masculine ladder: DER → DEN → DEM → DES. Feminine: DIE → DIE → DER → DER. Neuter: DAS → DAS → DEM → DES. Plural: DIE → DIE → DEN → DER."},
ein:{title:"Indefinite articles · ein/eine/ein",head:["Case","Masculine","Feminine","Neuter","Plural"],rows:[
["Nominativ","ein","eine","ein","—"],["Akkusativ","einen","eine","ein","—"],["Dativ","einem","einer","einem","—"],["Genitiv","eines","einer","eines","—"]],note:"There is no plural ein. For plural negative or possessive articles use keine / meine etc. Masc AKK takes -en; DAT takes -em/-er; GEN takes -es/-er."},
kein:{title:"Negative article · kein / keine",head:["Case","Masculine","Feminine","Neuter","Plural"],rows:[
["Nominativ","kein","keine","kein","keine"],["Akkusativ","keinen","keine","kein","keine"],["Dativ","keinem","keiner","keinem","keinen"],["Genitiv","keines","keiner","keines","keiner"]],note:"KEIN follows EIN in singular and has real plural endings. Mein/dein/sein/ihr/unser/euer/Ihr use the same type of endings. Dativ plural nouns usually add -n."},
poss:{title:"Possessive article · mein (also dein/sein/ihr/...), all cases",head:["Case","Masculine","Feminine","Neuter","Plural"],rows:[
["Nominativ","mein","meine","mein","meine"],["Akkusativ","meinen","meine","mein","meine"],["Dativ","meinem","meiner","meinem","meinen"],["Genitiv","meines","meiner","meines","meiner"]],note:"First choose whose: mein/dein/sein/ihr/unser/euer/Ihr. Then choose noun's case/gender, exactly as with KEIN. Example: mit meiner Kollegin; für meinen Chef."},
weak:{title:"Adjective endings · with der/die/das (weak)",head:["Case","Masc.","Fem.","Neut.","Plural"],rows:[
["Nominativ","der gute Chef","die gute Firma","das gute Team","die guten Kollegen"],["Akkusativ","den guten Chef","die gute Firma","das gute Team","die guten Kollegen"],["Dativ","dem guten Chef","der guten Firma","dem guten Team","den guten Kollegen"],["Genitiv","des guten Chefs","der guten Firma","des guten Teams","der guten Kollegen"]],note:"WEAK trick: adjective -e only in nominative singular (all three genders) and accusative feminine/neuter singular; otherwise -en. Article already carries the grammatical information."},
mixed:{title:"Adjective endings · with ein/kein/mein (mixed)",head:["Case","Masc.","Fem.","Neut.","Plural with kein/mein"],rows:[
["Nominativ","ein guter Chef","eine gute Firma","ein gutes Team","keine guten Kollegen"],["Akkusativ","einen guten Chef","eine gute Firma","ein gutes Team","keine guten Kollegen"],["Dativ","einem guten Chef","einer guten Firma","einem guten Team","keinen guten Kollegen"],["Genitiv","eines guten Chefs","einer guten Firma","eines guten Teams","keiner guten Kollegen"]],note:"MIXED trick: if EIN doesn't show gender/case (ein [M Nom], ein [N Nom/Akk]), adjective must show it: gutER/gutES. Otherwise -e in feminine Nom/Akk; -en in most other positions."},
strong:{title:"Adjective endings · without article (strong)",head:["Case","Masc.","Fem.","Neut.","Plural"],rows:[
["Nominativ","guter Kaffee","gute Arbeit","gutes Geld","gute Kollegen"],["Akkusativ","guten Kaffee","gute Arbeit","gutes Geld","gute Kollegen"],["Dativ","gutem Kaffee","guter Arbeit","gutem Geld","guten Kollegen"],["Genitiv","guten Kaffees","guter Arbeit","guten Geldes","guter Kollegen"]],note:"STRONG trick: adjective carries article-like endings when no article does, EXCEPT genitive masc/neuter adjectives take -en: guten Kaffees, guten Geldes."},
personal:{title:"Personal pronouns · all four cases",head:["Person","Nominativ","Akkusativ","Dativ","Genitiv (rare)"],rows:[
["I","ich","mich","mir","meiner"],["you (sg.)","du","dich","dir","deiner"],["he","er","ihn","ihm","seiner"],["she","sie","sie","ihr","ihrer"],["it","es","es","ihm","seiner"],["we","wir","uns","uns","unser"],["you (pl.)","ihr","euch","euch","euer"],["they","sie","sie","ihnen","ihrer"],["you (formal)","Sie","Sie","Ihnen","Ihrer"]],note:"Most useful: I = ich/mich/mir; he = er/ihn/ihm; she = sie/sie/ihr; formal you = Sie/Sie/Ihnen. Genitive personal pronouns are rare in everyday conversation."},
reflex:{title:"Reflexive pronouns",head:["Person","Akkusativ","Dativ"],rows:[
["ich","mich","mir"],["du","dich","dir"],["er/sie/es","sich","sich"],["wir","uns","uns"],["ihr","euch","euch"],["sie/Sie","sich","sich"]],note:"With another accusative object, reflexive pronoun is often Dativ: Ich wasche MIR DIE HÄNDE. Otherwise usually AKK: Ich interessiere MICH für die Stelle."},
relative:{title:"Relative pronouns · der/die/das",head:["Case","Masculine","Feminine","Neuter","Plural"],rows:[
["Nominativ","der","die","das","die"],["Akkusativ","den","die","das","die"],["Dativ","dem","der","dem","denen"],["Genitiv","dessen","deren","dessen","deren"]],note:"First match gender/number of the noun outside the relative clause, THEN case according to the relative verb/preposition. Dative plural = DENEN; genitive = DESSEN/DEREN (not des/der)."},
demonstrative:{title:"Demonstrative · dieser",head:["Case","Masculine","Feminine","Neuter","Plural"],rows:[
["Nominativ","dieser","diese","dieses","diese"],["Akkusativ","diesen","diese","dieses","diese"],["Dativ","diesem","dieser","diesem","diesen"],["Genitiv","dieses","dieser","dieses","dieser"]],note:"dies- follows definite article-type endings, e.g. dieser Mann, diesen Mann, diesem Mann, dieses Mannes. Likewise welcher/jener."},
prepAkk:{title:"Always Akkusativ",head:["Preposition","Memory cue","Example"],rows:[
["durch","through","durch den Park"],["für","for","für meinen Chef"],["gegen","against","gegen den Vorschlag"],["ohne","without","ohne einen Termin"],["um","around/at","um den Tisch"]],note:"Learn the chant: DURCH – FÜR – GEGEN – OHNE – UM. Also bis is typically accusative when accompanied by an article, but often appears without one or with another preposition."},
prepDat:{title:"Always Dativ",head:["Preposition","Meaning / cue","Example"],rows:[
["aus","from/out of","aus der Firma"],["außer","except","außer dem Kollegen"],["bei","at/with","bei meinem Arbeitgeber"],["mit","with","mit dem Zug"],["nach","after/to","nach dem Kurs"],["seit","since/for","seit einem Jahr"],["von","from/of","von meiner Kollegin"],["zu","to","zu dem Termin / zum Termin"]],note:"Chant: AUS – AUSSER – BEI – MIT – NACH – SEIT – VON – ZU. Include gegenüber + Dativ (dem Chef gegenüber)."},
prepGen:{title:"Common Genitiv prepositions (standard formal usage)",head:["Preposition","Meaning","Example"],rows:[
["wegen","because of","wegen des Termins"],["trotz","despite","trotz des Regens"],["während","during","während des Gesprächs"],["innerhalb","inside/within","innerhalb einer Woche"],["außerhalb","outside","außerhalb der Arbeitszeit"],["aufgrund","due to","aufgrund des Problems"],["anstatt / statt","instead of","statt eines Briefes"]],note:"For formal B2 Beruf writing use Genitiv after these, although some occur with Dativ in everyday speech."},
wechsel:{title:"Two-way prepositions · location vs destination",head:["Preposition","Wo? + Dativ","Wohin? + Akkusativ"],rows:[
["in","in der Bibliothek","in die Bibliothek"],["an","an der Wand","an die Wand"],["auf","auf dem Tisch","auf den Tisch"],["unter","unter dem Tisch","unter den Tisch"],["über","über dem Tisch","über den Tisch"],["vor","vor dem Gebäude","vor das Gebäude"],["hinter","hinter dem Haus","hinter das Haus"],["neben","neben dem Büro","neben das Büro"],["zwischen","zwischen den Büros","zwischen die Büros"]],note:"Ask LOCATION (Wo?) or DIRECTION / destination (Wohin?), not simply whether the action involves movement. Ich laufe im Park = Dativ."},
verbCases:{title:"Common verbs by case",head:["Akkusativ object","Dativ object","Dativ + Akkusativ"],rows:[
["sehen, haben, brauchen","helfen, danken","geben (person, thing)"],["fragen, anrufen, besuchen","antworten, folgen","zeigen (person, thing)"],["kennen, treffen, suchen","gehören, gefallen","schenken (person, thing)"],["lesen, kaufen, finden","zuhören, vertrauen","schicken (person, thing)"]],note:"A person is NOT automatically Dativ: fragen + AKK, anrufen + AKK; helfen + DAT. Learn each verb together with its case."},
fixed:{title:"Important fixed verb prepositions",head:["Verb + preposition","Case","Practical sentence"],rows:[
["warten auf","Akk","Ich warte auf die Antwort."],["denken an","Akk","Ich denke an den Termin."],["sich interessieren für","Akk","Ich interessiere mich für die Stelle."],["sich bewerben um","Akk","Ich bewerbe mich um eine Stelle."],["sich vorbereiten auf","Akk","Ich bereite mich auf die Prüfung vor."],["teilnehmen an","Dat","Ich nehme an dem Meeting teil."],["sprechen mit","Dat","Ich spreche mit dem Kunden."],["sich beschäftigen mit","Dat","Ich beschäftige mich mit dem Projekt."],["sich erkundigen nach","Dat","Ich erkundige mich nach dem Termin."],["sich kümmern um","Akk","Ich kümmere mich um das Problem."],["sich freuen auf / über","Akk","Ich freue mich auf den Urlaub / über das Geschenk."],["sich beschweren über / bei","Akk / Dat","über den Fehler; bei dem Anbieter"]],note:"Use the 3-part package: (sich) VERB + PREPOSITION + CASE. The case after a preposition does not determine whether the reflexive pronoun is mich or mir."},
sentence:{title:"Verb placement at a glance",head:["Clause","Formula","Example"],rows:[
["Main clause","Position 1 + finite verb (V2) + rest","Heute lerne ich Deutsch."],["Yes/no question","Finite verb first + subject + rest","Hast du heute Zeit?"],["W-question","Question word + finite verb + subject","Wann beginnt der Kurs?"],["Subordinate: weil/dass/ob","Connector + subject + rest + finite verb LAST","weil ich Deutsch lerne"],["Modal verb","Finite modal in V2 + infinitive LAST","Ich muss Deutsch lernen."],["Separable verb","Finite root in V2 + prefix LAST","Ich stehe früh auf."],["Two main clauses with denn","... , denn + subject + finite verb","Ich lerne, denn ich brauche Deutsch."],["Result: deshalb/trotzdem","deshalb + finite verb + subject","Deshalb lerne ich Deutsch."]],note:"V2 means second sentence UNIT, not second word. Subordinate clause at front: Weil ich lerne, bestehe ich die Prüfung (verb in first position of main-clause sequence immediately after comma)."},
connectors:{title:"Connector positions cheat sheet",head:["Connector","Pattern","Example"],rows:[
["weil / da","Verb LAST","weil ich arbeiten muss"],["obwohl","Verb LAST","obwohl ich müde bin"],["wenn / falls","Verb LAST","wenn ich Zeit habe"],["dass / ob","Verb LAST","dass er morgen kommt"],["bevor / nachdem","Verb LAST","bevor ich anfange"],["damit","Verb LAST","damit ich besser spreche"],["denn / aber / oder / und","Ordinary main-clause V2","denn ich habe Zeit"],["deshalb / trotzdem / außerdem","Connector + V2 (verb immediately follows)","Deshalb komme ich später."],["entweder ... oder","Two alternatives / main clauses","Entweder komme ich, oder ich rufe an."],["je ... desto / umso","Je verb LAST; desto verb after comparison","Je mehr ich übe, desto besser spreche ich."]],note:"Remember THREE types: (1) V-LAST: weil, dass, obwohl, wenn; (2) V2 after adverb: deshalb, trotzdem; (3) standard main clause: denn, aber, und, oder."},
negation:{title:"Negation comparison",head:["Word","Negates","Example"],rows:[
["nicht","verb/adjective/focused phrase","Das ist nicht wichtig."],["kein/e","noun with no definite article","Ich habe keine Zeit."],["nie / niemals","time/frequency","Ich war noch nie dort."],["nirgends / nirgendwo","place","Ich finde es nirgendwo."],["nirgendwohin","destination","Ich gehe nirgendwohin."],["niemand","person","Niemand hat angerufen."],["nichts","thing","Ich habe nichts verstanden."],["noch nicht","not yet","Ich bin noch nicht fertig."],["nicht mehr","no longer","Ich arbeite dort nicht mehr."],["weder ... noch","neither ... nor","Ich trinke weder Tee noch Kaffee."]],note:"Start with WHAT is negated: a noun → kein; an adjective/action → nicht; time → nie; place → nirgendwo; person → niemand; thing → nichts. Placement of NICHT depends on focus."},
comparison:{title:"Comparatives and paired expressions",head:["Basic","Comparative","Superlative"],rows:[
["gern","lieber","am liebsten"],["gut","besser","am besten"],["viel","mehr","am meisten"],["hoch","höher","am höchsten"],["groß","größer","am größten"],["schnell","schneller","am schnellsten"]],note:"Comparative + ALS: Mein Deutsch ist besser als früher. Equality: SO ... WIE: so gut wie. JE...DESTO uses comparative in BOTH clauses."},
time:{title:"Time expressions and verb position",head:["Expression","Use","Example"],rows:[
["seit + Dat","since/for still continuing","seit zwei Jahren"],["vor + Dat","ago","vor zwei Wochen"],["in + Dat (time)","from now","in einer Stunde"],["ab + Dat","starting from","ab nächstem Montag"],["während + Gen","during","während des Termins"],["bevor / nachdem","before / after clause: verb LAST","Nachdem ich gegessen habe, ..."],["bis / sobald","until / as soon as: verb LAST","Bis der Kurs beginnt, ..."]],note:"Seit = action has continued until now. Vor = finished time ago. Distinguish time prepositions from time-clause connectors."}
};
const lessons=[];let seq=0;
function add(section,title,level,when,decision,pattern,hook,examples,mistake,table,quiz){
 lessons.push({id:"g"+(++seq),section,title,level,when,decision,pattern,hook,examples,mistake,table,quiz});
}
const E=(de,en)=>[de,en];
const Q=(question,correct,w1,w2,w3,why)=>({question,correct,wrong:[w1,w2,w3],why:why||""});
/* CASES: first choose case, then article, then endings. */
add("cases","The four cases: the decision tree","A2","Every time you use an article or pronoun.","1. Who acts? NOM. 2. What/person is acted on? often AKK. 3. To whom? DAT. 4. Whose? GEN. 5. Check a verb/preposition that requires a case.","NOM: der Chef; AKK: den Chef; DAT: dem Chef; GEN: des Chefs.","DER–DEN–DEM–DES (masculine ladder). Feminine DIE–DIE–DER–DER; Neuter DAS–DAS–DEM–DES.",[E("Der Chef gibt dem Kunden den Bericht.","The manager gives the customer the report."),E("Das Auto des Chefs ist neu.","The manager's car is new.")],"A person is not always Dativ: Ich frage DEN Kunden.", "articles",Q("Ich helfe ___ Kollegen.","dem","den","der","des","helfen always takes Dativ."));
add("cases","All definite articles: der/die/das","A1","Choosing the correct article across all four cases.","Identify gender/plural, then select the required case; read the intersection of the table.","Nom der/die/das/die → Akk den/die/das/die → Dat dem/der/dem/den → Gen des/der/des/der","Memorise columns vertically, then make 4 example sentences using the SAME noun.",[E("Ich sehe den Chef.","I see the manager."),E("Ich spreche mit der Kollegin.","I am speaking with the female colleague.")],"Dativ plural usually adds -n to the NOUN: mit den Kollegen; exception when plural already ends -n/-s.","articles",Q("Wegen ___ Problems ...","des","dem","den","das","wegen + Genitiv in formal German."));
add("cases","All indefinite articles: ein/eine/ein","A1","Talking about one previously unspecified person or object.","Pick gender, then case. There is NO plural ein; use bare plurals or other articles.","ein / eine / ein (Nom) → einen / eine / ein (Akk) → einem / einer / einem (Dat) → eines / einer / eines (Gen)","Akkusativ masculine alone gets EINEN. DAT = EINEM/EINER. GEN = EINES/EINER.",[E("Ich habe einen Termin.","I have an appointment."),E("Ich spreche mit einer Kundin.","I am speaking with a customer.")],"Not: mit eine Kollegin; use mit einer Kollegin.","ein",Q("Wir haben ___ neuen Mitarbeiter.","einen","ein","einem","einer","Masculine Akk: einen."));
add("cases","All forms of kein and possessive mein","A2","Saying no/not any, or identifying who owns something.","KEIN and possessives follow the same ending pattern across all genders including plural.","kein / keine / kein / keine; meinen (Akk Masc); meinem (Dat Masc); meiner (Dat Fem); meinen (Dat Pl)","Think KEIN = EIN plus plural. Meine follows the same pattern as keine.",[E("Ich habe keine Erfahrung damit.","I don't have experience with that."),E("Ich spreche mit meinen Kollegen.","I speak with my colleagues.")],"Not: Ich habe nicht Zeit. Here use KEINE Zeit.","kein",Q("Ich freue mich über ___ neue Stelle.","meine","meiner","meinem","meinen","Stelle feminine Akkusativ after über in this meaning."));
add("cases","Genitiv: ownership & formal use","B1","Showing possession or after formal Genitiv prepositions.","Ask WESSEN? Often des + masculine/neuter noun -(e)s, der + feminine/plural.","das Projekt des Kunden · die Meinung der Kollegin","GEN M/N = DES + noun -(e)S. GEN F/PL = DER, no noun -s normally.",[E("Die Ergebnisse des Projekts sind gut.","The results of the project are good."),E("Wegen des Termins komme ich später.","Because of the appointment, I will come later.")],"Formal Genitive vs conversational von + Dativ: die Meinung von meinem Kollegen.","articles",Q("Die Unterlagen ___ Firma sind hier.","der","des","dem","die","Firma feminine Genitiv = der."));
add("cases","N-Deklination: der Kollege","B1","A small but important group of masculine nouns.","Many animate masculine nouns add -(e)n in singular AKK, DAT and GEN.","der Kollege → den Kollegen → dem Kollegen → des Kollegen","KOLLEGE–KUNDE–STUDENT–MENSCH often gain -n/-en outside NOM.",[E("Ich helfe dem Kollegen.","I help the colleague."),E("Ich frage den Kunden.","I ask the customer.")],"Some nouns are irregular e.g. der Name → den Namen → des Namens.","articles",Q("Ich arbeite mit einem ___.","Kollegen","Kollege","Kollegem","Kolleges","Dativ masculine n-declension: Kollegen."));
add("cases","Special verbs that take Akkusativ","A2","Some people think persons always take Dativ; that's wrong.","Learn verb + case in pairs: fragen, anrufen, besuchen, treffen, sehen, brauchen, kennen, suchen + AKK.","Ich frage DEN Chef; ich rufe MEINEN Kollegen an.","Remember FRAGEN and ANRUFEN = AKK, despite referring to people.",[E("Ich rufe meinen Arzt an.","I call my doctor."),E("Ich besuche meine Kollegin.","I visit my colleague.")],"Wrong: Ich frage dem Chef.","verbCases",Q("Sie fragt ___ Mitarbeiter.","den","dem","des","der","fragen requires Akkusativ."));
add("cases","Special verbs that take Dativ","A2","Certain common verbs directly require Dativ without a preposition.","helfen, danken, antworten, folgen, gefallen, gehören, vertrauen, zuhören + DAT.","Ich helfe IHM; ich antworte DEM Kunden.","H-D-A-F-G-G: helfen, danken, antworten, folgen, gefallen, gehören.",[E("Ich antworte dem Kunden.","I answer the customer."),E("Die Arbeit gefällt mir.","I like the work.")],"antworten DEM Kunden; but jemanden FRAGEN is Akkusativ.","verbCases",Q("Diese Stelle gefällt ___.","mir","mich","ich","mein","gefallen + Dativ pronoun."));
add("cases","Dativ person + Akkusativ thing","B1","When transferring information, objects or favors.","Common verbs: geben, senden, schicken, zeigen, erklären, schenken; recipient DAT and thing AKK.","Subj + finite verb + DAT(person) + AKK(thing)","WEM gets it? DAT. WAS is transferred? AKK.",[E("Ich erkläre dem Kunden das Problem.","I explain the problem to the customer."),E("Der Chef schickt uns den Vertrag.","The boss sends us the contract.")],"When objects are pronouns, order can change: Ich gebe ES IHM.","verbCases",Q("Ich erkläre ___ Chef den Fehler.","dem","den","der","des","Recipient (wem?) is Dativ."));
/* ADJECTIVES & ENDINGS */
add("endings","Adjectives after der/die/das","A2","Whenever the adjective comes before a noun WITH a definite article.","Use -e in Nom singular, Akk singular feminine/neuter; otherwise -en.","der gutE Chef → den gutEN Chef → dem gutEN Chef → des gutEN Chefs","WEAK = E in only FIVE slots (Nom M/F/N + Akk F/N). EN everywhere else.",[E("Der neue Mitarbeiter beginnt heute.","The new employee starts today."),E("Ich helfe dem neuen Mitarbeiter.","I help the new employee.")],"After sein the adjective has NO ending: Der Mitarbeiter ist neu.","weak",Q("mit dem ___ Mitarbeiter","neuen","neue","neuer","neues","DAT + definite article = -en."));
add("endings","Adjectives after ein/kein/mein","A2","When the article does not always show gender.","Where EIN has no ending, the adjective shows gender: ein gutER Chef / ein gutES Team.","ein gutER Chef · eine gutE Firma · ein gutES Team · einen gutEN Chef","MIXED: the adjective fills missing information in EIN. Otherwise often -en.",[E("Ich suche einen neuen Job.","I am looking for a new job."),E("Wir haben ein neues Projekt.","We have a new project.")],"Not: ein gute Chef; the adjective must say -ER.","mixed",Q("ein ___ Projekt","neues","neuen","neuem","neue","Neuter Nom/Akk with ein → -es."));
add("endings","Adjectives with no article","B1","With bare nouns such as guter Kaffee, frische Luft, neue Projekte.","The adjective itself carries most case/gender endings; Genitive M/N takes -en.","gutER Kaffee, gutEN Kaffee, gutEM Kaffee, gutEN Kaffees","STRONG = adjective plays the role of the missing article. Gen M/N exception = -en.",[E("Gute Kommunikation ist wichtig.","Good communication is important."),E("Wir brauchen frische Ideen.","We need fresh ideas.")],"Not: mit gutem Kollegen? Correct for bare singular: mit gutem Kollegen (where appropriate).","strong",Q("Wir arbeiten mit ___ Material.","gutem","guten","guter","gutes","Material neuter DAT without article = -em."));
add("endings","The 3 endings patterns side by side","B1","Choosing the right adjective ending in an exam.","First ask: Is there DER? EIN/MEIN/KEIN? Or no article? Then case/gender.","der gutE Chef · ein gutER Chef · gutER Chef","DER does the grammar work → weak. EIN misses some endings → mixed. NO ARTICLE → strong.",[E("Der neue Kollege hat einen neuen Vertrag.","The new colleague has a new contract."),E("Gute Kommunikation hilft im Team.","Good communication helps within the team.")],"Only adjectives BEFORE nouns decline: Die Aufgabe ist schwierig (no ending).","mixed",Q("Ich sehe ___ neuen Kollegen.","einen","ein","einem","eines","ein + masculine Akk = einen; adjective -en."));
add("endings","Noun genders: helpful clues and exceptions","A1","When learning a new noun.","Memorise every noun with its article and plural. Suffixes give useful hints but have exceptions.","-ung/-heit/-keit/-schaft/-ion mostly DIE; -chen/-lein DAS; -ismus/-ling often DER","Feminine: DIE BewerbUNG, DIE MöglichKEIT. Neuter: DAS MädCHEN.",[E("Die Entscheidung ist schwierig.","The decision is difficult."),E("Das Unternehmen wächst.","The company is growing.")],"Many gender rules are tendencies, not guarantees; learn article + word + plural together.","articles",Q("___ Bewerbung ist fertig.","Die","Der","Das","Den","-ung nouns are typically feminine."));
add("endings","Plural patterns and Dativ plural","A2","Nouns in the plural or after Dativ plural articles.","Common plural endings: -e/-er/-n/-en/-s/zero; many plurals need Umlaut. Add -n in DAT plural if possible.","die Kollegen → mit den Kollegen · die Kinder → mit den Kindern","Dativ plural: DEN + noun ending N (unless already -n/-s).",[E("Ich spreche mit den Kunden.","I speak with the customers."),E("Ich helfe den Kindern.","I help the children.")],"Plural is lexical: do not infer it from one ending alone.","articles",Q("Ich spreche mit den ___.","Kindern","Kinder","Kindes","Kind","Dativ plural Kinder → Kindern."));
add("endings","Comparative and superlative","A2","Comparing jobs, projects, choices and conditions.","Comparative -er + als; equal so ... wie; superlative am ...-sten.","gut → besser → am besten · gern → lieber → am liebsten","MORE → -er ALS; SAME → so ... WIE; BEST → am ...sten.",[E("Dieses Angebot ist besser als das andere.","This offer is better than the other."),E("Am liebsten arbeite ich im Team.","I most like working in a team.")],"Not: besser wie in standard comparison; use besser als.","comparison",Q("Der Kurs ist besser ___ letztes Jahr.","als","wie","zu","ob","Comparative + als."));
/* PRONOUNS */
add("pronouns","ich / mich / mir and all persons","A1","Choosing the right personal pronoun.","Subject NOM; direct object AKK; Dativ with specific verbs/prepositions; genitive rarely.","ich/mich/mir; du/dich/dir; er/ihn/ihm; sie/sie/ihr; wir/uns/uns","Remember I→ICH, me seen→MICH, to me→MIR.",[E("Sie sieht mich.","She sees me."),E("Sie hilft mir.","She helps me.")],"Not: Er hilft mich. HELFEN takes DAT.","personal",Q("Kannst du ___ helfen?","mir","mich","ich","mein","helfen + Dativ."));
add("pronouns","sein / ihr / unser: whose?","A2","Expressing ownership; converting I said to he/she said.","Owner selects stem: mein/dein/sein/ihr/unser/euer/ihr/Ihr; noun gender/case selects ending.","sein Chef, seinen Chef, seinem Chef · ihre Chefin, ihrer Chefin","HIS = sein, HER = ihr; ending follows the noun, not the owner.",[E("Er spricht mit seinem Chef.","He speaks with his boss."),E("Sie spricht mit ihrer Chefin.","She speaks with her boss.")],"sein means his/its; ihr can mean her, their, or your (formal Ihr capitalised).","poss",Q("Er telefoniert mit ___ Kollegin.","seiner","seine","seinem","seinen","Kollegin fem DAT → seiner."));
add("pronouns","Reflexive: mich vs mir","B1","When the subject performs an action affecting itself.","Most reflexive verbs AKK: mich/dich/sich; if there is another Akk object, reflexive pronoun can be DAT.","Ich wasche MICH. Ich wasche MIR die Hände.","Two objects? Hands = AKK, so person = MIR (DAT).",[E("Ich interessiere mich für die Stelle.","I am interested in the position."),E("Ich putze mir die Zähne.","I brush my teeth.")],"Don't mix case of reflexive pronoun with case after its preposition.","reflex",Q("Ich wasche ___ die Hände.","mir","mich","ich","mein","die Hände are the Akk object; mir is Dativ."));
add("pronouns","Relative clauses: der/die/das/dem/denen","B1","Describing a noun with a subordinate clause.","Match gender/number of noun; choose CASE based on verb/preposition within relative clause; verb last.","der Kollege, DER kommt; der Kollege, DEN ich sehe; der Kollege, DEM ich helfe","Relative = noun's gender, relative clause's case; verb LAST.",[E("Der Kollege, dem ich helfe, ist nett.","The colleague whom I help is kind."),E("Das Team, dessen Chef neu ist, wächst.","The team whose boss is new is growing.")],"Dativ plural DENEN; Genitiv DESSEN/DEREN, not just des/der.","relative",Q("Die Kollegen, ___ ich helfe, sind nett.","denen","den","die","deren","Dativ plural relative pronoun is denen."));
add("pronouns","dieser / diese / dieses / welcher","B1","Pointing to a specific noun or asking which one.","Decline dieser and welcher like definite article endings.","diesER Chef · diesEN Chef · diesEM Chef · diesES Chefs","DER ending can be attached to DIES- and WELCH-.",[E("Mit diesem Kollegen arbeite ich gern.","I like working with this colleague."),E("Welche Stelle meinst du?","Which job do you mean?")],"Akk masc is diesen, not dieser.","demonstrative",Q("Ich spreche mit ___ Mann.","diesem","diesen","dieser","dieses","mit + DAT Masc = diesem."));
add("pronouns","da(r)- and wo(r)- words","B2","Referring to a thing or asking about a thing with a preposition.","wo + prep (question); da + prep (reference); insert -r- before vowel.","warten auf → worauf / darauf · sprechen über → worüber / darüber","WORAUF? = on what? DARAUF = on it. Persons: auf ihn, not darauf.",[E("Worauf wartest du? Ich warte darauf.","What are you waiting for? I am waiting for it."),E("Darüber müssen wir sprechen.","We need to discuss that.")],"For people, keep preposition + person pronoun: auf sie, mit ihm.","fixed",Q("___ wartest du? Auf den Bericht.","Worauf","Darauf","Wohin","Womit","Question referring to a thing + auf = worauf."));
/* PREPOSITIONS */
add("preps","Always Akkusativ prepositions","A2","Preposition forces the case regardless of location.","durch, für, gegen, ohne, um + AKK; bis often without an article.","für DEN Chef; ohne EINEN Termin","Chant: DURCH FÜR GEGEN OHNE UM.",[E("Das Geschenk ist für meinen Kollegen.","The present is for my colleague."),E("Wir sprechen über den Vertrag.","We discuss the contract.")],"Über is a two-way preposition; für is always Akk.","prepAkk",Q("Das Geschenk ist für ___ Kollegen.","den","dem","des","der","für always Akkusativ."));
add("preps","Always Dativ prepositions","A2","Preposition forces Dativ.","aus, außer, bei, mit, nach, seit, von, zu, gegenüber + DAT.","mit DEM Chef; bei DER Firma; zu DEM Termin → zum Termin","Chant: AUS AUSSER BEI MIT NACH SEIT VON ZU.",[E("Ich arbeite bei einem Unternehmen.","I work at a company."),E("Ich fahre mit dem Bus.","I travel by bus.")],"Not: mit den Bus. MIT + DAT.","prepDat",Q("Ich fahre mit ___ Zug.","dem","den","der","des","mit always Dativ."));
add("preps","Formal Genitiv prepositions","B2","Formal writing, reports and exams.","wegen, trotz, während, innerhalb, außerhalb, aufgrund, statt/anstatt + GEN.","wegen DES Problems · trotz DES Regens · während DER Besprechung","B2 formal: WEGEN/TROTZ/WÄHREND + Genitiv.",[E("Wegen des Termins komme ich später.","Due to the appointment I will arrive later."),E("Trotz der Probleme lief das Projekt gut.","Despite the problems, the project went well.")],"Colloquial Dativ can occur, but learn Genitiv for formal B2 writing.","prepGen",Q("Trotz ___ Wetters gehen wir raus.","des schlechten","dem schlechten","das schlechte","den schlechten","trotz + Genitiv; das Wetter → des Wetters."));
add("preps","Wechselpräpositionen: Wo vs Wohin","A2","For place and destination with in/an/auf/unter/über/vor/hinter/neben/zwischen.","WO/location → DAT; WOHIN/destination → AKK.","Ich bin in DER Firma. Ich gehe in DIE Firma.","WO = DAT; WOHIN = AKK. Movement alone is not the test.",[E("Ich laufe im Park.","I am running in the park."),E("Ich laufe in den Park.","I run into the park.")],"In both sentences there is motion; only the second expresses destination.","wechsel",Q("Ich gehe in ___ Büro.","das","dem","des","der","Wohin? Neuter Akk → das Büro."));
add("preps","Verb + fixed preposition + case","B1","When a verb requires a particular preposition.","Learn them in 3 parts: warten auf+AKK, teilnehmen an+DAT, denken an+AKK, bitten um+AKK.","Ich nehme AN EINEM Kurs teil; ich warte AUF DIE Antwort","Don't memorize teilnehmen alone; say TEILNEHMEN AN + DAT aloud.",[E("Ich nehme an einem Meeting teil.","I participate in a meeting."),E("Ich bitte um eine Rückmeldung.","I request a response.")],"Not: Ich nehme in einem Meeting teil.","fixed",Q("Ich nehme ___ einem Kurs teil.","an","auf","um","mit","teilnehmen an + Dativ."));
add("preps","Reflexive verbs with prepositions","B1","Talking about interests, preparation, applications and complaints.","sich interessieren für+AKK, sich freuen auf/über+AKK, sich bewerben um+AKK, sich beschäftigen mit+DAT, sich erkundigen nach+DAT.","Subject + finite verb + mich/sich + prep + article/object","Memorise each COMPLETE PACKAGE: mich + BEWERBEN UM + AKK.",[E("Ich bereite mich auf die Prüfung vor.","I prepare for the exam."),E("Ich beschäftige mich mit dem Projekt.","I work on the project.")],"Reflexive mich is not the object of mit. MIT still requires Dativ.","fixed",Q("Ich beschäftige mich ___ dem Projekt.","mit","für","um","auf","sich beschäftigen mit + Dativ."));
add("preps","Time: seit / vor / in / ab","A2","Talking about duration, ago, future time, start time.","seit+DAT (ongoing), vor+DAT (ago), in+DAT (from now), ab+DAT (starting).","seit ZWEI JAHREN; vor EINER WOCHE; in ZWEI TAGEN","SEIT = still happening. VOR = ago. IN = from now.",[E("Ich lerne seit zwei Jahren Deutsch.","I have studied German for two years."),E("Vor zwei Monaten habe ich angefangen.","I started two months ago.")],"Wrong: Ich lerne vor zwei Jahren Deutsch if it continues today.","time",Q("Ich lerne ___ drei Monaten Deutsch.","seit","vor","nach","um","seit + Dativ expresses ongoing duration."));
/* VERBS */
add("verbs","Present tense: regular and irregular","A1","Talking about habitual actions and present/future plans.","ich -e, du -st, er -t, wir -en, ihr -t, sie -en; irregular stem changes possible.","arbeiten: ich arbeite, du arbeitest, er arbeitet","E–ST–T–EN–T–EN. For du and er/sie/es, check stem vowels: fahren → du fährst.",[E("Ich arbeite heute im Büro.","I work in the office today."),E("Du sprichst gut Deutsch.","You speak German well.")],"Some verb stems require an extra -e-: du arbeitest.","sentence",Q("Er ___ Deutsch.","spricht","spreche","sprechen","sprichst","sprechen has a vowel change: er spricht."));
add("verbs","Perfekt: haben or sein + Partizip II","A2","Talking about past events in conversation.","haben/sein (conjugated V2) + ... + Partizip II at END.","Ich HABE gearbeitet. Ich BIN gefahren.","HABEN for most verbs; SEIN for many changes of location/state and sein/bleiben/werden. Check the verb.",[E("Ich habe den Bericht geschrieben.","I wrote the report."),E("Ich bin nach Berlin gefahren.","I traveled to Berlin.")],"fahren can use haben with a direct object: Ich habe das Auto gefahren.","sentence",Q("Ich ___ gestern nach Köln gefahren.","bin","habe","werde","war","change of location → bin gefahren."));
add("verbs","Präteritum & three principal forms","B1","Past narratives, written reports and irregular verbs.","Infinitiv – Präteritum – Partizip II; strong verbs may change stem.","gehen – ging – gegangen (sein); schreiben – schrieb – geschrieben (haben)","Learn verbs in sets of THREE plus HABEN/SEIN.",[E("Früher arbeitete ich in Indien.","I used to work in India."),E("Der Chef schrieb gestern eine E-Mail.","The manager wrote an email yesterday.")],"Modal verbs and sein/haben often use Präteritum in speech: war, hatte, konnte.","sentence",Q("gehen – ___ – gegangen","ging","gang","gehte","gegangen","Irregular Präteritum of gehen = ging."));
add("verbs","Plusquamperfekt & nachdem","B1","An action that happened BEFORE another past action.","hatte/war + Partizip II; nachdem often introduces earlier action.","Nachdem ich den Bericht geschrieben HATTE, schickte ich ihn ab.","Past before past = Plusquamperfekt.",[E("Nachdem ich gefrühstückt hatte, ging ich zur Arbeit.","After I had breakfast, I went to work."),E("Ich war schon gegangen, als er ankam.","I had already left when he arrived.")],"Do not use plusquamperfekt for every past event; it marks earlier past.","connectors",Q("Nachdem ich gegessen ___, ging ich los.","hatte","habe","werde","hätte","Earlier past: hatte gegessen."));
add("verbs","Futur I / future with present","B1","Expressing a future prediction, promise or plan.","werden in V2 + infinitive LAST. Often Präsens + future time works too.","Ich WERDE morgen ARBEITEN.","MORGEN + present is usually enough; WERDE can emphasize prediction/promises.",[E("Ich werde Ihnen morgen antworten.","I will reply to you tomorrow."),E("Morgen habe ich einen Termin.","Tomorrow I have an appointment.")],"Don't use werden + zu: Ich werde arbeiten, not werde zu arbeiten.","sentence",Q("Ich ___ morgen kommen.","werde","habe","bin","hatte","Futur I uses werden + infinitive."));
add("verbs","Modal verbs, two-verb sentences","A2","Expressing ability, obligation, permission, wishes.","modal conjugated in V2 + main infinitive at END WITHOUT zu.","Ich MUSS morgen ARBEITEN. Wir KÖNNEN das MACHEN.","Modal is the finite verb; the other verb sits at the end.",[E("Ich möchte morgen früher gehen.","I would like to leave earlier tomorrow."),E("Sie müssen das Formular ausfüllen.","You must fill in the form.")],"Wrong: Ich muss zu gehen.","sentence",Q("Ich muss morgen früh ___.","aufstehen","aufzustehen","aufgestanden","aufstehe","Modal verbs use bare infinitive."));
add("verbs","Separable & inseparable verbs","A2","Position of prefixes and Partizip II.","Main clause: conjugated root V2, separable prefix LAST. Infinitive: prefix stays attached.","Ich FANGE heute AN. Ich möchte ANFANGEN.","Prefix jumps to the END in a statement; with zu, prefix+zu+verb: anzufangen.",[E("Ich rufe den Kunden zurück.","I call the customer back."),E("Ich versuche, früh aufzustehen.","I try to get up early.")],"Inseparable be-/ver-/er- verbs do not separate: Ich verstehe dich.","sentence",Q("Ich versuche, früh ___.","aufzustehen","zu aufstehen","aufstehen","aufgestanden","Separable aufstehen → aufzustehen."));
add("verbs","Passiv: action and state","B1","Formal reports, processes, and instructions at work.","Vorgangspassiv: werden + Partizip II. Zustandspassiv: sein + Partizip II.","Der Vertrag WIRD geprüft (process). Der Vertrag IST geprüft (result).","WERDEN = happening; SEIN = completed state.",[E("Die Unterlagen werden morgen verschickt.","The documents will be sent tomorrow."),E("Die Tür ist geschlossen.","The door is closed.")],"Don't confuse Zustandspassiv with Perfekt: ist gegangen is Perfekt, not state passive.","sentence",Q("Der Bericht ___ gerade geschrieben.","wird","ist","hat","war","Ongoing action: wird geschrieben."));
add("verbs","Konjunktiv II: polite & hypothetical","B1","Polite workplace requests, wishes, suggestions.","würde + infinitive; hätte, wäre, könnte, müsste, sollte and other forms.","Könnten Sie bitte ...? Ich würde gern ...","Polite: KÖNNTEN/SOLLTE/WÜRDE. Wishes: HÄTTE/WÄRE.",[E("Könnten Sie mir die Unterlagen schicken?","Could you send me the documents?"),E("Wenn ich mehr Zeit hätte, würde ich mehr lernen.","If I had more time, I would study more.")],"Avoid würde sein where wäre is more natural: Ich wäre froh.","sentence",Q("Ich ___ gern mehr Zeit.","hätte","hatte","haben","habe","Hypothetical wish: hätte."));
add("verbs","lassen + infinitive","B2","Getting something done, permission or arrangements.","lassen conjugated V2 + object + bare infinitive at END.","Ich LASSE mein Auto REPARIEREN.","lassen like a modal: no ZU before the second verb.",[E("Ich lasse meinen Laptop reparieren.","I am having my laptop repaired."),E("Lassen Sie mich bitte ausreden.","Please let me finish speaking.")],"Wrong: Ich lasse meinen Laptop zu reparieren.","sentence",Q("Ich lasse das Gerät ___.","reparieren","zu reparieren","repariert","reparierte","lassen + bare infinitive."));
add("verbs","Infinitiv with zu: exact placement","B1","After verbs such as versuchen/planen, adjectives and nouns.","zu directly before simple infinitive; INSIDE separable verb between prefix and stem.","Ich versuche, Deutsch ZU LERNEN. Ich versuche, früh AUFZUSTEHEN.","Normal: ZU + verb. Separable: prefix + ZU + root. Modal: usually NO ZU.",[E("Es ist wichtig, regelmäßig zu üben.","It is important to practise regularly."),E("Ich habe keine Zeit, das heute zu erledigen.","I have no time to do this today.")],"After modal verbs no zu: Ich muss arbeiten.","connectors",Q("Ich versuche, früher ___.","anzufangen","zu anfangen","anfangen","angefangen","With trennbar anfangen: anzufangen."));
add("verbs","Participles & nominalisation","B2","Reading formal descriptions and turning verbs into nouns.","Partizip I: infinitive+d + adjective ending; nominalised infinitive starts uppercase.","der arbeitende Kollege · die abgeschlossene Aufgabe · beim Lernen","Participles describe nouns; nominalised verbs behave like nouns: DAS Lernen.",[E("Die abgeschlossenen Projekte werden archiviert.","The completed projects are archived."),E("Beim Lernen mache ich Notizen.","I take notes while studying.")],"Participle adjectives still decline: die abgeschlossenen Projekte.","weak",Q("Beim ___ trinke ich Wasser.","Lernen","lernen","lernt","gelernt","Nominalised verb after beim is capitalised."));
/* WORD ORDER */
add("order","Main clause: verb second (V2)","A1","Every German main-clause statement.","Exactly one element in position 1; conjugated verb position 2; subject can follow verb.","HEUTE + LERNE + ICH Deutsch. ICH + LERNE + heute Deutsch.","Position 2 = second CHUNK, not second written word.",[E("Morgen habe ich einen Termin.","Tomorrow I have an appointment."),E("Wegen des Wetters fahre ich mit dem Bus.","Because of the weather, I travel by bus.")],"Wrong: Morgen ich habe einen Termin.","sentence",Q("Morgen ___ ich länger arbeiten.","muss","ich muss","müssen","gemusst","Finite modal verb must be V2."));
add("order","Subordinate clause: conjugated verb LAST","A2","After weil, dass, obwohl, wenn, ob, bevor, nachdem, damit.","Connector + subject + objects/time + finite verb at the END.","weil + ich + heute + ARBEITEN MUSS","WEIL sends finite verb to the END. Main clause after a fronted subordinate starts with finite verb.",[E("Ich gehe früher, weil ich einen Termin habe.","I leave earlier because I have an appointment."),E("Weil ich einen Termin habe, gehe ich früher.","Because I have an appointment, I leave earlier.")],"Wrong: Weil ich habe einen Termin.","sentence",Q("Weil ich krank ___, bleibe ich zu Hause.","bin","ich bin","sein","habe","weil clause ends with conjugated verb."));
add("order","Questions, commands and inversion","A2","Asking yes/no or question-word questions and making requests.","Yes/no: VERB + subject. W-question: question word + VERB + subject. Imperative: COME!/KOMMEN SIE!","HAST du Zeit? WANN HAST du Zeit? KOMMEN Sie bitte.","Question opens with finite verb unless a W-word comes first.",[E("Haben Sie morgen Zeit?","Do you have time tomorrow?"),E("Kommen Sie bitte um neun Uhr.","Please come at nine o'clock.")],"Indirect questions are different: Wissen Sie, wann der Kurs beginnt?","sentence",Q("___ Sie morgen Zeit?","Haben","Sie haben","Hat","Habt","Yes/no question starts with finite verb."));
add("order","TEKAMOLO: time/reason/manner/place","B1","Ordering several details naturally.","Usual neutral order: Temporal → Kausal → Modal → Lokal.","Ich fahre MORGEN WEGEN DES TERMINS MIT DEM ZUG NACH KÖLN.","TE–KA–MO–LO: WHEN – WHY – HOW – WHERE.",[E("Ich arbeite heute wegen des Termins länger im Büro.","I work longer in the office today because of the appointment."),E("Morgen fahre ich mit dem Zug nach Köln.","Tomorrow I travel by train to Cologne.")],"This is a useful default, not a rigid law; focus and pronouns may alter order.","sentence",Q("Heute ___ ich mit dem Bus zur Arbeit.","fahre","ich fahre","fahren","gefahren","V2 still applies despite TEKAMOLO."));
add("order","Two verbs: sentence bracket (Satzklammer)","A2","Modal, Perfekt, separable verbs, passive and future.","Conjugated verb in V2; nonfinite part / prefix at end of MAIN clause.","Ich HABE den Bericht GESCHRIEBEN. Ich RUFE dich AN.","Think verb as two bookends: conjugated part near front, rest at end.",[E("Ich werde Sie morgen anrufen.","I will call you tomorrow."),E("Wir müssen den Termin verschieben.","We have to move the appointment.")],"Subordinate clauses place the finite verb at the end of the verb group (with exceptions e.g. Ersatzinfinitiv).","sentence",Q("Ich habe den Vertrag gestern ___.","unterschrieben","unterschreiben","unterschrieb","unterschreibe","Perfekt Partizip II at end."));
add("order","Objects: pronoun and noun ordering","B2","When you have both Akkusativ and Dativ objects.","Two nouns: often DAT before AKK. Two pronouns: often AKK before DAT. A pronoun usually precedes a full noun.","Ich gebe DEM CHEF DEN BERICHT. Ich gebe IHN IHM.","Two nouns: DAT → AKK. Two pronouns: AKK → DAT.",[E("Ich schicke meinem Kollegen den Vertrag.","I send my colleague the contract."),E("Ich schicke ihn ihm.","I send it to him.")],"This is a neutral default; emphasis can change ordering.","sentence",Q("Which is the usual two-pronoun order?","Ich gebe es ihm.","Ich gebe ihm es.","Ich ihm gebe es.","Ich es ihm gebe.","Both pronouns in main clause: Akk before Dat."));
add("order","Indirect questions with ob / wann / wie","B1","Politely asking for details at work.","Main clause + comma + question word/ob + subject + rest + finite VERB LAST.","Können Sie mir sagen, WANN der Kurs BEGINNT?","Indirect questions use a subordinate clause: verb goes LAST.",[E("Wissen Sie, ob die Unterlagen angekommen sind?","Do you know whether the documents have arrived?"),E("Können Sie sagen, wann der Termin beginnt?","Can you say when the appointment starts?")],"Wrong: ob sind die Unterlagen angekommen.","connectors",Q("Wissen Sie, wann der Kurs ___?","beginnt","beginnen","er beginnt","begannst","Indirect question: finite verb last."));
add("order","Relative sentences: verb last","B1","Adding information about a person/thing.","Noun + comma + relative pronoun + ... + finite verb LAST.","Der Kollege, DEM ich HELFE, ist neu.","Find noun gender, THEN relative pronoun case within clause.",[E("Die Firma, bei der ich arbeite, ist groß.","The company I work for is large."),E("Der Mitarbeiter, den ich angerufen habe, kommt später.","The colleague I called is arriving later.")],"Not: die Firma, bei die ich arbeite. BEI + Dat and Firma feminine → der.","relative",Q("Die Firma, bei ___ ich arbeite, ist groß.","der","die","das","den","bei + Dativ; Firma feminine → der."));
/* CONNECTORS */
add("connectors","Three connector families and verb position","B1","Distinguish why German connectors have different structures.","1 weil/obwohl/dass → verb LAST. 2 denn/aber/und/oder → normal main V2. 3 deshalb/trotzdem/außerdem → verb immediately after.","WEIL ICH ZEIT HABE. DENN ICH HABE ZEIT. DESHALB HABE ICH ZEIT.","LAST / NORMAL / INVERSION = 3 bins.",[E("Ich lerne, weil ich einen Test habe.","I study because I have a test."),E("Ich habe einen Test. Deshalb lerne ich.","I have a test. Therefore I study.")],"Wrong: Deshalb ich lerne.","connectors",Q("Ich bin krank. Deshalb ___ ich zu Hause.","bleibe","ich bleibe","bleiben","geblieben","Deshalb in first position → verb follows."));
add("connectors","weil / denn / da / deshalb","B1","Explaining reasons, consequences and causality.","weil/da + clause verb LAST; denn + normal main clause; deshalb/darum + verb immediately after.","Ich bleibe, WEIL ich ARBEITEN MUSS. Ich muss arbeiten, DENN ich habe Arbeit.","WEIL=last; DENN=normal; DESHALB=V2 inversion.",[E("Ich bleibe zu Hause, weil ich krank bin.","I stay home because I am sick."),E("Ich bin krank, deshalb bleibe ich zu Hause.","I am sick, so I stay home.")],"Da often introduces a known reason; formal registers also use aufgrund+Gen.","connectors",Q("Ich lerne Deutsch, denn ich ___ in Deutschland.","arbeite","ich arbeite","arbeiten","gearbeitet","denn introduces a main clause."));
add("connectors","obwohl / trotzdem / dennoch","B1","Showing unexpected contrast.","obwohl + finite verb LAST; trotzdem/dennoch + conjugated verb immediately after.","OBWOHL ich müde BIN, lerne ich. TROTZDEM LERNE ich.","OBWOHL = verb LAST. TROTZDEM = verb SECOND.",[E("Obwohl ich müde bin, gehe ich schwimmen.","Although I am tired, I go swimming."),E("Ich bin müde. Trotzdem gehe ich schwimmen.","I am tired. Nevertheless I go swimming.")],"Not: Obwohl ich bin müde.","connectors",Q("Trotzdem ___ ich jeden Tag Deutsch.","lerne","ich lerne","lernen","gelernt","Trotzdem starts the clause, so finite verb follows."));
add("connectors","entweder ... oder","A2","Choosing between two alternatives.","It connects words/phrases OR complete main clauses. Each full clause follows V2.","Entweder LERNE ich, oder ich GEHE schwimmen.","ENTWEDER (first chunk) + VERB immediately after.",[E("Entweder fahre ich mit dem Zug, oder ich nehme den Bus.","Either I go by train or I take the bus."),E("Ich trinke entweder Tee oder Kaffee.","I drink either tea or coffee.")],"entweder doesn't always force verb right after it if it is inside the clause.","connectors",Q("Entweder ___ ich zu Hause, oder ich gehe raus.","bleibe","ich bleibe","bleiben","geblieben","At clause start: Entweder + V2 verb."));
add("connectors","weder ... noch / sowohl ... als auch","B1","Rejecting two things or including both.","weder A noch B = neither; sowohl A als auch B = both.","Ich trinke WEDER Kaffee NOCH Tee. Ich spreche SOWOHL Deutsch ALS AUCH Englisch.","WEDER excludes; SOWOHL includes.",[E("Ich habe weder Zeit noch Geld.","I have neither time nor money."),E("Ich arbeite sowohl selbstständig als auch im Team.","I work both independently and in a team.")],"Don't add extra nicht to weder ... noch in ordinary usage.","connectors",Q("Ich trinke ___ Tee noch Kaffee.","weder","sowohl","entweder","nicht nur","weder ... noch = neither/nor."));
add("connectors","nicht nur ... sondern auch / zwar ... aber","B1","Adding emphasis or conceding a contrast.","nicht nur A, sondern auch B; zwar A, aber B (each clause stays V2).","NICHT NUR A SONDERN AUCH B; ZWAR A ABER B.","SONDERN AUCH adds; ZWAR admits, ABER contrasts.",[E("Sie hat nicht nur Erfahrung, sondern auch Fachwissen.","She has not only experience but also expertise."),E("Der Job ist zwar stressig, aber interessant.","The job is stressful but interesting.")],"sondern is not the same as aber; sondern corrects or adds after nicht nur.","connectors",Q("Er spricht nicht nur Deutsch, ___ auch Englisch.","sondern","aber","oder","noch","not only ... but also = nicht nur ... sondern auch."));
add("connectors","einerseits ... andererseits","B2","Structuring pro/con arguments in an exam.","Both are adverbs in first position, so each is followed by a finite V2 verb.","EINERSEITS IST ... ANDERERSEITS HAT ...","Two sides: EINE = one side; ANDERE = other side.",[E("Einerseits spart Homeoffice Zeit, andererseits fehlt der Kontakt.","Working from home saves time, but social contact is missing."),E("Einerseits ist die Arbeit interessant, andererseits ist sie stressig.","On one hand the work is interesting, on the other it is stressful.")],"Wrong: Einerseits Homeoffice ist gut.","connectors",Q("Andererseits ___ es Nachteile.","hat","es hat","haben","hätte sein","Adverb in position 1 → finite verb in position 2."));
add("connectors","je ... desto / umso","B2","Explaining how two quantities change together.","JE + comparative + subordinate clause finite VERB LAST; DESTO/UMSO + comparative + finite VERB + subject.","JE MEHR ich LERNE, DESTO BESSER SPRECHE ich.","JE sends verb LAST; DESTO puts it after comparison.",[E("Je öfter ich übe, desto sicherer spreche ich.","The more often I practise, the more confidently I speak."),E("Je mehr Erfahrung man hat, umso einfacher wird es.","The more experience one has, the easier it becomes.")],"Wrong: Je ich mehr übe, desto ich besser spreche.","connectors",Q("Je mehr ich übe, desto besser ___ ich.","spreche","ich spreche","sprechen","gesprochen","After desto + comparison, finite verb follows."));
add("connectors","um ... zu vs damit","B1","Explaining PURPOSE.","um ... zu (same subject for main and infinitive action); damit + subject + conjugated verb LAST (can be a different subject).","Ich lerne, UM den Test ZU BESTEHEN. Ich helfe dir, DAMIT du BESTEHST.","UM ZU = same doer, DAMIT allows two different doers.",[E("Ich lerne Deutsch, um beruflich weiterzukommen.","I learn German to advance professionally."),E("Ich erkläre es dir, damit du es verstehst.","I explain it so that you understand.")],"Wrong: Ich helfe dir, um du es zu verstehen.","connectors",Q("Ich lerne Deutsch, ___ die Prüfung zu bestehen.","um","damit","weil","denn","um ... zu + infinitive for same subject purpose."));
add("connectors","ohne ... zu / ohne dass / statt ... zu","B2","Describing without doing something or doing something instead.","Same subject: ohne/statt + ... + zu Infinitiv; other subject: ohne dass/statt dass + clause verb LAST.","Ich gehe, OHNE mich ZU VERABSCHIEDEN.","ohne zu = without doing; statt zu = instead of doing.",[E("Er geht, ohne sich zu verabschieden.","He leaves without saying goodbye."),E("Ich lerne Deutsch, statt fernzusehen.","I learn German instead of watching TV.")],"For different agents, use ohne dass: Er ging, ohne dass ich es merkte.","connectors",Q("Sie geht, ___ sich zu verabschieden.","ohne","weil","denn","damit","ohne ... zu is correct with same subject."));
add("connectors","Infinitiv mit zu vs without zu","B1","Choosing whether the second verb needs zu.","Many verbs: versuchen/planen/hoffen + zu; modal verbs, lassen, gehen/kommen + infinitive without zu.","Ich VERSUCHE, zu LERNEN. Ich MUSS LERNEN. Ich LASSE es REPARIEREN.","Zu is NOT universal: modals and lassen use bare infinitive.",[E("Ich hoffe, bald eine Stelle zu finden.","I hope to find a job soon."),E("Ich kann gut schwimmen.","I can swim well.")],"Separables: aufstehen → aufzustehen, not zu aufstehen.","connectors",Q("Ich plane, früher ___.","aufzustehen","aufstehen","zu aufstehen","aufgestanden","After planen, zu; with separable → aufzustehen."));
add("connectors","als / wenn / wann / ob","B1","Choosing when, whenever, if or whether.","ALS = single past; WENN = condition/repeat; WANN = time question; OB = whether.","ALS ich klein WAR; WENN ich Zeit HABE; WANN der Kurs BEGINNT; OB ich KOMMEN KANN","ALS = a past occasion; WENN = if/repeated; WANN asks time; OB asks yes/no fact.",[E("Als ich in Indien lebte, arbeitete ich dort.","When I lived in India, I worked there."),E("Ich weiß nicht, ob der Termin stattfindet.","I don't know whether the appointment will take place.")],"Wann belongs to time questions and indirect time questions, not general if clauses.","connectors",Q("Ich weiß nicht, ___ die Firma heute geöffnet ist.","ob","wenn","als","wann","Whether = ob."));
add("connectors","bevor / nachdem / während / sobald / bis","B2","Sequencing events accurately.","All introduce subordinate clauses with finite verb LAST; nachdem can combine Plusquamperfekt and Präteritum.","BEVOR ich GEHE; NACHDEM ich GEGESSEN HATTE; SOBALD ich FERTIG BIN","Time clause = verb LAST. Sequence determines which past tense.",[E("Bevor ich den Kunden anrufe, lese ich die Unterlagen.","Before I call the client, I read the documents."),E("Sobald der Bericht fertig ist, schicke ich ihn ab.","As soon as the report is ready, I send it.")],"während + noun uses Genitiv formal; während + clause sends verb to end.","time",Q("Ich rufe an, sobald ich Zeit ___.","habe","ich habe","haben","hatte ich","sobald clause = verb last."));
/* NEGATION */
add("negation","Choose nicht or kein","A1","Making a statement negative.","Noun without a definite reference → KEIN. Adjective/adverb/verb/specific focus → NICHT.","KEINE ZEIT, KEIN AUTO; NICHT müde, NICHT heute","NOUN? KEIN. Adjective/action? NICHT.",[E("Ich habe keine Zeit.","I don't have time."),E("Der Termin ist nicht wichtig.","The appointment isn't important.")],"Do not say Ich habe nicht Zeit; use keine Zeit.","negation",Q("Ich habe ___ Erfahrung.","keine","nicht","nie","nichts","Erfahrung is a noun → keine."));
add("negation","Where does nicht go?","B1","You need to negate the entire sentence or just a part.","With adjectives: before adjective. With prepositional phrase: before PP. With separable verb: before prefix. Whole clause: typically late in middle field.","Das ist NICHT teuer. Ich fahre NICHT mit dem Bus. Ich rufe heute NICHT an.","NICHT sits before the part it negates; otherwise towards the end, but BEFORE the last verb/prefix.",[E("Ich fahre heute nicht zur Arbeit.","I am not going to work today."),E("Ich arbeite nicht heute, sondern morgen.","I work not today, but tomorrow.")],"Not universal: nicht always at end is wrong: Ich kann nicht kommen.","negation",Q("Das ist ___ einfach.","nicht","kein","keine","niemand","Before adjective einfach → nicht."));
add("negation","nie / niemals / nirgendwo / nirgends","A2","Negating time/frequency vs place.","NIE/NIEMALS = never, NIRGENDWO/NIRGENDS = nowhere (where), NIRGENDWOHIN = to nowhere.","Ich habe dort NIE gearbeitet. Ich finde meinen Schlüssel NIRGENDWO.","NIE = WHEN never, NIRGENDS = WHERE nowhere.",[E("Ich war noch nie in dieser Stadt.","I have never been to this city."),E("Meine Schlüssel sind nirgendwo zu finden.","My keys are nowhere to be found.")],"niemals means never, niemand means nobody; not the same.","negation",Q("Ich bin dort ___ gewesen.","nie","nirgendwohin","niemand","keine","Time/frequency = nie."));
add("negation","niemand / nichts / keiner / nirgendwohin","B1","Negating a person, thing, or movement destination.","NIEMAND = no person; NICHTS = no thing; KEINER = none/no one; NIRGENDWOHIN = no destination.","Niemand IST da. Ich habe NICHTS gehört. Ich gehe NIRGENDWOHIN.","WHO = niemand; WHAT = nichts; WHERE TO = nirgendwohin.",[E("Niemand hat geantwortet.","Nobody replied."),E("Ich habe nichts verstanden.","I understood nothing.")],"Use niemanden in Akkusativ when appropriate: Ich kenne niemanden.","negation",Q("Ich habe ___ verstanden.","nichts","niemand","nirgendwohin","kein","Negating a thing = nichts."));
add("negation","noch nicht vs nicht mehr","B1","Describing pending and stopped activities.","NOCH NICHT = not yet. NICHT MEHR = no longer.","Ich arbeite NOCH NICHT. Ich arbeite NICHT MEHR dort.","NOCH = still waiting; MEHR = ended.",[E("Der Bericht ist noch nicht fertig.","The report isn't finished yet."),E("Ich arbeite nicht mehr bei dieser Firma.","I no longer work at that company.")],"nicht mehr differs from nie: a stopped activity vs never done.","negation",Q("Ich bin ___ nicht fertig.","noch","mehr","nie","kein","noch nicht = not yet."));
add("negation","weder ... noch and kaum","B2","Negative pairs and nearly not.","WEDER A NOCH B = neither; KAUM = hardly/barely (not a plain negator).","Ich habe WEDER Zeit NOCH Geld. Ich habe KAUM Zeit.","WEDER–NOCH negates both; KAUM means little/almost none.",[E("Wir haben weder Personal noch Budget.","We have neither staff nor budget."),E("Ich habe kaum geschlafen.","I have barely slept.")],"Don't add nicht to weder ... noch as standard grammar.","negation",Q("Ich habe ___ Zeit noch Geld.","weder","sowohl","nicht nur","entweder","neither = weder ... noch."));
/* WORKPLACE */
add("beruf","Professional emails: polite request","B2","Requesting documents, clarification or an appointment.","Könnten Sie bitte + object + infinitive? · Ich würde mich freuen, wenn + verb LAST.","KÖNNTEN Sie mir ... SCHICKEN? Ich würde mich freuen, WENN ...","Polite triangle: Könnten Sie ...? Ich wäre Ihnen dankbar ... Ich freue mich auf ...",[E("Könnten Sie mir bitte die Unterlagen zusenden?","Could you please send me the documents?"),E("Ich wäre Ihnen für eine Rückmeldung dankbar.","I would be grateful for a reply.")],"Not: Ich würde freuen; use Ich würde mich freuen.","sentence",Q("___ Sie mir bitte helfen?","Könnten","Können mich","Hätten","Würden helfen","Polite Konjunktiv II of können = könnten."));
add("beruf","Complaints and problems: formal German","B2","Complaining professionally without sounding aggressive.","Ich möchte darauf hinweisen, dass + verb LAST. Leider ist ... . Ich bitte um + AKK.","Ich möchte darauf HINWEISEN, DASS die Lieferung FEHLT.","Be factual: problem → consequence → requested solution.",[E("Leider entspricht das Produkt nicht der Beschreibung.","Unfortunately the product does not match the description."),E("Ich bitte Sie um eine zeitnahe Lösung.","I request a timely solution.")],"bitten UM + Akk; entsprechen + Dativ: entspricht DER Beschreibung.","fixed",Q("Das Gerät entspricht nicht ___ Beschreibung.","der","die","den","das","entsprechen requires Dativ."));
add("beruf","B2 discussion: advantages/disadvantages","B2","Discussing Homeoffice, teamwork and workplace questions.","Einerseits + V2, andererseits + V2. Zwar + V2, aber + V2. Abschließend + V2.","EINERSEITS IST ..., ANDERERSEITS FEHLT ...","Use 4 moves: Opinion → Reason → Example → Conclusion.",[E("Einerseits bietet Homeoffice Flexibilität, andererseits fehlt der persönliche Austausch.","Working from home offers flexibility but lacks personal interaction."),E("Meiner Meinung nach ist eine Mischung sinnvoll.","In my opinion a mix makes sense.")],"Meiner Meinung nach is a first-position phrase; finite verb must immediately follow.","connectors",Q("Meiner Meinung nach ___ Homeoffice praktisch.","ist","Homeoffice ist","sein","hat ist","Finite verb after the introductory phrase."));
add("beruf","B2 conditional & concession","B2","Proposals, decisions and alternatives at work.","wenn/falls/sofern + verb LAST; obwohl/auch wenn + verb LAST; sonst + verb V2.","FALLS etwas PASSIERT, INFORMIERE ich Sie.","If/falls = condition; obwohl/auch wenn = despite; sonst = otherwise.",[E("Falls der Termin ausfällt, informieren Sie mich bitte.","If the appointment is cancelled, please inform me."),E("Auch wenn es schwierig ist, versuchen wir es.","Even if it is difficult, we try.")],"Avoid using ob for if in conditional statements.","connectors",Q("___ ich Zeit habe, rufe ich Sie an.","Wenn","Ob","Wann","Als","If condition = wenn."));
add("beruf","Nominal style and formal texts","B2","Reports, workplace notices and technical descriptions.","Verb → noun: prüfen → die Prüfung; entscheiden → die Entscheidung; durchführen → die Durchführung.","Wegen DER VERZÖGERUNG ... · Nach DER PRÜFUNG ...","For formal writing: verb idea → noun + preposition + required case.",[E("Nach der Prüfung erhalten Sie die Ergebnisse.","After the examination you receive results."),E("Aufgrund der Verzögerung verschiebt sich der Termin.","Due to the delay the appointment is postponed.")],"Nominalisation often changes article/case; don't just capitalise a verb mechanically.","prepGen",Q("Aufgrund ___ Problems kommt es zu Verzögerungen.","des","dem","das","den","aufgrund + Genitiv."));
add("beruf","Passiv in instructions and processes","B2","Describing what is done rather than who does it.","werden + Partizip II, subject is affected thing. von + Dativ for actor.","Der Bericht WIRD geprüft. Die Maschine WIRD gewartet.","Instructions: WAS WIRD GETAN? = passive process.",[E("Die Dokumente werden elektronisch gespeichert.","The documents are stored electronically."),E("Der Vertrag wird vom Geschäftsführer unterschrieben.","The contract is signed by the managing director.")],"With von the actor is Dativ: vom Geschäftsführer.","sentence",Q("Die Unterlagen ___ geprüft.","werden","haben","sind haben","sollen werden","Plural subject + passive werden."));
add("beruf","Verbs with prepositions in job applications","B2","Common phrases in job advertisements and interviews.","sich bewerben um+AKK; verfügen über+AKK; Erfahrung haben mit+DAT; interessiert sein an+DAT.","Ich BEWERBE MICH UM die Stelle. Ich VERFÜGE ÜBER Erfahrung.","LEARN UNITS: bewerben um; verfügen über; interessiert sein an.",[E("Ich verfüge über mehrere Jahre Berufserfahrung.","I have several years of professional experience."),E("Ich bin an der Stelle interessiert.","I am interested in the role.")],"Ich interessiere mich FÜR die Stelle but Ich bin AN der Stelle interessiert.","fixed",Q("Ich verfüge ___ gute Deutschkenntnisse.","über","an","um","mit","verfügen über + Akkusativ."));
add("beruf","Sprachbausteine: choose article and case","B2","Gap-filling tasks in professional contexts.","Locate verb/preposition first → determine case → noun gender/number → article/adjective ending.","MIT + DAT + DIE FIRMA → mit DER Firma.","In gap-fill questions, search LEFT for the trigger and RIGHT for the noun.",[E("Wir danken Ihnen für Ihre Rückmeldung.","We thank you for your reply."),E("Während des Gesprächs wurden Fragen geklärt.","Questions were clarified during the conversation.")],"Don't choose the article by noun gender alone; case matters.","articles",Q("Wir sprechen mit ___ neuen Kollegin.","der","die","den","dem","mit Dativ feminine → der; adjective neuen."));
add("beruf","B2 connectors in a formal report","B2","Organising reasons, consequences and contrast clearly.","aufgrund+GEN / daher+V2 / dennoch+V2 / obwohl+verb LAST / sofern+verb LAST.","Aufgrund DES AUSFALLS ... DAHER VERSCHIEBEN WIR ...","Separate connectors by verb-position family before writing.",[E("Aufgrund des Ausfalls wird der Termin verschoben.","Due to the outage the appointment is postponed."),E("Die Kosten sind hoch. Dennoch lohnt sich die Investition.","The costs are high. Nevertheless the investment is worthwhile.")],"daher/dennoch lead to V2 inversion, not subordinate verb-last.","connectors",Q("Dennoch ___ wir das Projekt fort.","setzen","wir setzen","setzen wir sind","gesetzt","Dennoch in position 1 → conjugated verb in V2."));
add("beruf","Presentation and speaking patterns","B2","Giving a structured two-minute talk at B2 Beruf level.","Heutzutage + V2; Meiner Meinung nach + V2; Ein Vorteil ist, dass + verb LAST; Abschließend + V2.","HEUTZUTAGE ARBEITEN viele ... EIN VORTEIL IST, DASS ...","4 sentences to remember: Today → Advantage → Example → My opinion.",[E("Heutzutage arbeiten viele Menschen im Homeoffice.","Nowadays many people work from home."),E("Ein Vorteil ist, dass man Zeit sparen kann.","An advantage is that you can save time.")],"Wrong: Ein Vorteil ist, dass man kann Zeit sparen.","connectors",Q("Ein Vorteil ist, dass man Zeit sparen ___.","kann","man kann","können","könnte man","dass clause: conjugated verb last."));
window.B2_GRAMMAR_COMPLETE={sections,tables,lessons,version:"4.1"};
